{"id": "EUVD-2026-55814", "enisaUuid": "ca6763b7-0eff-386a-a1d8-104a628480e3", "description": "A flaw was found in Data Science Pipelines (DSP). An attacker with namespace editor privileges can bypass security hardening by submitting a malicious Argo Workflow through the V1 API path. This allows the API server to create pods with elevated privileges, acting as a 'confused deputy' on behalf of the attacker. Successful exploitation grants the attacker node-root access, enabling arbitrary code execution and full control over the underlying node.", "datePublished": "2026-08-10T20:44:37", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T11:10:02", "baseScore": 7.6, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:L/A:L", "references": ["https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:53261", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:53262", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:53263", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:60520", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:65126", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:84734", "https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-18621", "https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2510327"], "aliases": ["GHSA-6wxg-hpw6-m2x7", "CVE-2026-18621"], "assigner": "redhat", "epss": 0.52, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "41349cd6-f70e-3448-8f16-370a944dfb17", "product": {"name": "Red Hat OpenShift AI 3.4", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1784924951"}, {"id": "6a5e5dff-7563-375d-8c0f-2745827afd32", "product": {"name": "Red Hat OpenShift AI 3.4", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1787173417"}, {"id": "aa35eb5d-d922-3745-8f6f-e5bccbaf2bc6", "product": {"name": "Red Hat OpenShift AI 3.4", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1791866195"}, {"id": "d50d70ad-db9e-342e-b70c-875b3078ae8c", "product": {"name": "Red Hat OpenShift AI 2.25", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1785189934"}, {"id": "ec50f6c5-f4d4-3eea-ab46-ce20f